    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>Most claims have a turning point: a large loss, a low first offer, a delay that drags on, or a denial. Those are the moments to consider professional help.</li>
<li>Earlier is usually easier. Evidence is freshest right after the damage, before repairs and cleanup.</li>
<li>Small, clear-cut claims often do not need a public adjuster.</li>
<li>In Texas, public adjuster compensation is capped at 10% of the settlement, contracts must use TDI-approved terms, and you can rescind within 72 hours of signing.</li>
<li>A public adjuster represents you, not the insurer. They are not attorneys and cannot promise a specific result.</li>
